# 19. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

After implementation, test the actual end-to-end workflows.

### Test A — Institution and case linkage

Create or use a clearly labelled test institution and associate cases with it.

Verify that the institution profile shows all associated cases.

### Test B — Cross-bureau overlap

Associate one active PGRC case and one relevant RB case with the same institution.

Verify that the system identifies the shared institution and produces a persistent potential-overlap alert according to the configured rules.

### Test C — False-positive handling

Associate unrelated complaints with the same institution.

Verify that the system does not automatically declare them duplicates and provides sufficient information for authorized review.

### Test D — Case transfer

Transfer a case between Bureaus/Cells.

Verify that the current assignment changes and the previous assignment remains visible in the action history.

### Test E — Case status

Change a case status and verify that the dashboard, case detail, institution profile, and relevant reports remain consistent.

### Test F — Search and filtering

Search by case ID, institution ID, Bureau/Cell, region, category, status, and date range.

Verify that combined filters work correctly.

### Test G — Timeline alerts

Create test cases with approaching and overdue expected disposal dates.

Verify the alert logic against the configured rules.

### Test H — ML classification

Submit a complaint through the actual prediction pipeline.

Verify that the returned category is produced by the real model and that prediction errors are handled correctly.

### Test I — Action history

Change case ownership, status, and relevant details.

Verify that timestamps and historical actions remain intact.

### Test J — Security

Verify that unauthorized users cannot perform restricted backend actions simply by bypassing the frontend.

### Test K — Dashboard consistency

Compare dashboard counts with the corresponding case records and report queries.

### Test L — Regression

Verify that existing routes, navigation, forms, responsive layouts, and previously working functionality continue to work.

Use automated tests where available and document any test that could not be performed.

